            "review_title": "Review at fuAsian - Cafe & Restaurant ( Halal Food)",
            "review_text": "Tourist26840288784\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam10 contributions\n1\nWhen It's Good, It's Good. When It's Bad, It's Awful\nOct 2026 • Solo\nApparently this restaurant likes to delete bad reviews🤣 Some of the dishes are quite nice, but when it is bad, it is TERRIBLE. I ordered Chicken Alfredo from here, and it was extremely bad-especially for the price that they are selling it for. The chicken was hard and overcooked. Completely unseasoned-- something you would find in a hospital. The sauce is definitely not parmesan based-- it is one of the basic cream sauces that you can pick up at a grocery store. The noodles were overcooked. It tastes as bland as it looks on my pics. The restaurant has the audacity to sell this for 159k on Grab--you can find a superior chicken/noodle/cream sauce dish at the Circle K or MiniMart for 39k. In addition, there is absolutely nothing special about the 'Special Tea' that they serve. It is plain tea with sugar and a kumquat slice. You get better for cheaper on the road.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nStick to the Indian/Asian food. DO NOT ORDER WESTERN FOOD. Western food is made to appeal to old British people. COMPLETELY UNSEASONED.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten October 11, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
